  "id": "compound-eye",
  "term": "compound eye",
  "definition": "A compound eye is an arthropod eye made up of many facets, each associated with retinal elements around a crystalline cone. In historical accounts of vision, it was discussed as producing sight either from many tiny points that combine into one image or from many small complete images.",
